A1. It's a short lane that hasn't one of these. (Two words.) ~ ASHCAN
A6. One of the "Health and Happiness" boys. ~ WEALTH
A12. No garage is complete without one. ~ TOOL
A14. A large continent. ~ ASIA
A16. Something farmers do after they sow their wild oats. ~ REAP
A18. A pryer. ~ LEVER
A21. African golf balls. ~ DICE
A23. A laundered shirt. ~ RAG
A24. Kings and queens. ~ ROYALTY
A26. Something necessity and most lawyers know very little about. ~ LAW
A27. The beginning of every Eskimo. ~ ES
A28. A débutante's favorite fruit. ~ DATE
A29. With women this means to look around. ~ SHOP
A31. Pronoun. ~ ME
A32. A difficult thing to make flivvers do. ~ START
A34. One way of getting what's coming to you. ~ SUE
A36. To kick against authority. ~ REBEL
A38. An irritating thing to get in the eye. ~ BUST
A40. A festival. ~ FETE
A41. Something most men carry home on New Year's Eve. ~ BUN
A42. To take place in Scandinavia. ~ OCCUR
A43. Foundation of flivvers. ~ TIN
A45. Something husbands do if they're given too much rope. ~ SKIP
A47. A Teutonic god. ~ ODIN
A50. What most racing cars are built for. ~ SPEED
A52. Cat fight. ~ TEA
A54. When people fall out of bed this is what they wake up in. ~ ANGER
A56. Is your old man! ~ SO
A57. A kind of beer (?). ~ NEAR
A59. It's safer to give Her this on the phone. ~ RING
A61. Pronoun. ~ ME
A62. The human thing to do. ~ ERR
A64. The Congressional record. ~ ASININE
A66. A contraction for "it is." ~ TIS
A67. What few schoolgirl complexions are. ~ REAL
A69. When you want a diamond this is what you get. ~ SPADE
A70. Arts. ~ ARTS
A71. This indicates the direction of an ill wind. ~ VANE
A73. A Ku Klux necktie. ~ ROPE
A75. To rest in peace. ~ REPOSE
A76. Something that people start crossing Vertical and finish crossing Horizontal. ~ STREET

D2. A fellow who horns in at dances. ~ STAG
D3. Dance. ~ HOP
D4. A group of dough makers (abbr.). ~ CO
D5. To portion out. ~ ALLOT
D7. Couples who marry in aeroplanes soon come back to this. ~ EARTH
D8. A conjunction. ~ AS
D9. The brown derby. ~ LID
D10. Something a snake is little else but. ~ TAIL
D11. To seize, as a bandit in Chicago. ~ ARREST
D13. Topsy's girl friend. ~ EVA
D15. What seven black pearls are. ~ JEWELS
D17. You'll arrive here if you go west far enough. ~ EAST
D19. Sometimes these have very bright pupils. ~ EYES
D20. Otherwise. ~ ELSE
D22. What Caesar did before he saw and conquered. ~ CAME
D24. A rodent exclamation. ~ RATS
D25. Long ago. ~ YORE
D28. Pie-eyed. ~ DRUNKEN
D30. Most people are in the dark about these kind of parties. ~ PETTING
D33. To use improperly. ~ ABUSE
D35. So's your aunt's brother! ~ UNCLE
D37. Existing. ~ BEING
D39. This goes around a lot. ~ TOP
D40. Away from. ~ FRO
D44. Something married men can't do with their rights. ~ ASSERT
D46. A fortunate thing to be struck with. ~ IDEA
D48. An inhabitant of Denmark. ~ DANE
D49. Dolled up. ~ DRESSY
D51. Small hole in the skin. ~ PORE
D52. You can't travel far without taking one of these. ~ TRIP
D53. Dry. ~ ARID
D55. To give forth. ~ EMIT
D58. English dumb-bells. ~ ASSES
D60. Inactive. ~ INERT
D63. Something wild wives do. ~ RAVE
D65. An old hobby. ~ NAG
D66. This leaves in the spring. ~ TREE
D68. Something a person loses when he stands up. ~ LAP
D70. Imitate. ~ APE
D72. This means no in England. ~ NO
D74. A conjunction. ~ OR


